@startuml
title Project frame rate: importing, choosing a rate, opening an old project

actor User
participant EditorView
participant TimelineEditor
participant FrameRate
participant Timeline
participant "Playback / render / mixer" as Play

== import into an empty timeline ==
User -> TimelineEditor : drop media
TimelineEditor -> FrameRate : Plausible(asset.SourceRate)
alt not RateChosen and no clips and a plausible rate
  TimelineEditor -> Timeline : Rate = that rate
end
TimelineEditor -> TimelineEditor : clip.DurSec = asset.DurationSec (never scaled)

== choose the project frame rate ==
User -> EditorView : pick 25 fps
EditorView -> TimelineEditor : SetRate(25)
TimelineEditor -> Timeline : SetTimelineRateCommand (undoable)\nRate = 25, RateChosen = true
note right : clips keep their place and length;\nonly the frame grid and export rate change

== play / render / mix ==
Play -> Play : srcTime = SrcIn + (t - StartSec) x Speed

== open a project saved before ==
TimelineEditor -> Timeline : RealTimeMediaMigration (FormatVersion < 2)
note right : clip.Speed x= SourceRate / Rate\nwhere they differed
@enduml
